          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "For each of the following, find the smallest positive integer ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "x",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " that makes the expression a square number.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p77-q20-notation-note",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Note that in this case, ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "17x",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " means ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "17\\times x",
              "display": false
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p77-q20-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$17x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=17$",
          "worked": "A square has even powers in its prime factorisation. Since $17$ is prime, the smallest multiplier is $x=17$.\n$$\\begin{align*}17x&=17\\times17\\\\17x&=289\\\\17x&=17^2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p77-q20-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$12x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=3$",
          "worked": "$$12=2^2\\times3$$\nThe power of $3$ is odd, so the smallest multiplier is $x=3$.\n$$\\begin{align*}12x&=12\\times3\\\\12x&=36\\\\12x&=6^2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p77-q20-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$15x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=15$",
          "worked": "$$15=3\\times5$$\nBoth prime powers are odd, so the smallest multiplier is $x=3\\times5=15$.\n$$\\begin{align*}15x&=15\\times15\\\\15x&=225\\\\15x&=15^2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p77-q20-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$16x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=1$",
          "worked": "$$16=2^4=4^2$$\nThe prime power is already even, so the smallest positive multiplier is $x=1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p77-q20-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$288x$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=2$",
          "worked": "$$288=2^5\\times3^2$$\nOnly the power of $2$ is odd, so the smallest multiplier is $x=2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}288x&=288\\times2\\\\288x&=576\\\\288x&=24^2\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      }
    ]
  },
